  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 405.33 Waivers",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 405.33 Waivers.\n\n(a) Any applicant or supplier of water who would be adversely impacted by the strict application of a rule in this part and who wishes to request a waiver of the rule shall do so in accordance with Env-Dw 202.\n\n(b) Waivers shall not be granted for criteria which pose a direct risk to public health, such as including, but not limited to, proper well construction, multiple wells where required, water quality standards, or the integrity of the water storage tank(s).\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for Env-Dw 405) #10612, eff 6-1-14; ss by #14158, eff 12-25-24 (formerly Env-Dw 405.35)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html"
